{"id": "EUVD-2026-28573", "enisaUuid": "716a8750-b998-3e04-9833-66d0b03acdb9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/page_alloc: clear page->private in free_pages_prepare()\n\nSeveral subsystems (slub, shmem, ttm, etc.) use page->private but don't\nclear it before freeing pages.  When these pages are later allocated as\nhigh-order pages and split via split_page(), tail pages retain stale\npage->private values.\n\nThis causes a use-after-free in the swap subsystem.  The swap code uses\npage->private to track swap count continuations, assuming freshly\nallocated pages have page->private == 0.  When stale values are present,\nswap_count_continued() incorrectly assumes the continuation list is valid\nand iterates over uninitialized page->lru containing LIST_POISON values,\ncausing a crash:\n\n  KASAN: maybe wild-memory-access in range [0xdead000000000100-0xdead000000000107]\n  RIP: 0010:__do_sys_swapoff+0x1151/0x1860\n\nFix this by clearing page->private in free_pages_prepare(), ensuring all\nfreed pages have clean state regardless of previous use.", "datePublished": "2026-05-08T13:11:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:16:26", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7790ab165713b79b1617ce659742ceb3a859d05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3edb8ebbf79b9016040e8f3421d723ae3d542b32", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9719e32a67b4b00b3c9b133e8b5ffa72a26b67b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23b82b7a26182ad840ae67d390d7ec9771e8c00f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d757c793853ec5483eb41ec2942c300b8fa720fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac1ea219590c09572ed5992dc233bbf7bb70fef9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6fh9-96ww-pvwq", "CVE-2026-43303"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "020482a6-51f2-354a-8178-6f84c02c5c3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b8000ae185cb068adbda5f966a3835053c85fd4 <ac1ea219590c09572ed5992dc233bbf7bb70fef9"}, {"id": "1e7efb3d-afaf-3380-a35a-78ce39877980", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.16"}, {"id": "21b5992d-9e12-34ff-a037-c9ce7f69d430", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2981ab6d-420d-3d41-83b8-309e501c4abd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.176"}, {"id": "52b8a467-6314-3fbb-96a5-29128e73e45e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b8000ae185cb068adbda5f966a3835053c85fd4 <e7790ab165713b79b1617ce659742ceb3a859d05"}, {"id": "675091c7-6ff5-3c54-827b-0ad9812df477", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.93"}, {"id": "7a16d287-d7dc-35a0-a4d8-e7708b68242c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.143"}, {"id": "97b0b0d0-1e30-3121-9a30-8a568647262b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.6"}, {"id": "ade13c80-7d29-32da-b2a9-37c2a89e88f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "af405beb-3890-3232-813d-02508ce4eb1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b8000ae185cb068adbda5f966a3835053c85fd4 <d757c793853ec5483eb41ec2942c300b8fa720fb"}, {"id": "c05c0cc2-9c0b-33fc-9590-7e9906275036", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b8000ae185cb068adbda5f966a3835053c85fd4 <3edb8ebbf79b9016040e8f3421d723ae3d542b32"}, {"id": "edc0578d-6049-392f-ba15-1af4318d2028", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.18"}, {"id": "fa46d375-3c31-35f8-83e9-6b2590a71331", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b8000ae18